{"kind":"request","text":"Fourteenth-round review of the deployment note at exact head 7f7b3644f01c0c7e798b8dd7f3aaeb4c82bac07f, artifact ee5dec2d8815330272c48c2dd3dcae3921b9046b. One subject.\n\nBefore the specifics, a change in how I want you to spend the round. Three of my last four blockers were Git mechanisms I asserted without running — the blob parent, the force-with-lease, the tree gitlink — and the fourth was a \"cannot happen\" argument. Prose review is not what has been catching those; your plumbing probes are. So if you have to choose, probe rather than read, and treat every sentence in this file that describes what Git does as unverified until you have run it. I have marked the new ones below.\n\nThe Git claims I have now made and you should distrust. That a profile *commit* whose tree carries the ruleset retains it against gc when the ledger is the only ref — I measured this, but I measured my own mechanism, which is exactly the pattern that produced the last three. That parent-role validation by object type is even possible cheaply, i.e. that an auditor can tell a ledger entry from a profile bundle from a sequence commit from a submitter candidate without unbounded traversal. And that rejecting a root with any ledger entry reachable anywhere in its parent graph is computable at all — reachability over a whole parent graph is not obviously bounded, and I have specified a check without asking what it costs on a long ledger.\n\nThe base-chaining rule is new and unprobed. Each entry takes its accounted predecessor's E as its base and the auditor verifies by walking one step back. I have not tested what happens at the root, where base must equal the genesis-declared initial head, nor whether \"the genesis-declared initial head\" is actually a thing the genesis descriptor carries — I have asserted that it is. If it is not, the root case has no anchor and the whole chain is unbound at exactly one end.\n\nOn refs=: the length-prefixed encoding is stated but I have not written an example with a delimiter-bearing name, so the format may not survive contact with one. And the cross-actor rule now says a mismatched ref gets an unauthorised-ref outcome \"against its creator\" — I have not established that the creator of a ref is determinable at all, which the whole remedy depends on.\n\nLast: I removed entries=n on your reasoning and I think you are right, but check that nothing downstream still counts on it, since removing a field is the mirror of the surviving-old-sentence pattern I keep producing.\n\nReport APPROVED or CHANGES-REQUESTED against this exact head with verbatim full event ids.","body":{"conditions":"Review notes/2026-08-07-deployment.md at exact head 7f7b3644f01c0c7e798b8dd7f3aaeb4c82bac07f. Prefer plumbing probes to prose review. Judge closed or open: the profile bundle commit replacing the impossible blob parent, including self-containment for executability; base bound to the accounted predecessor's E with the root anchored to a genesis-declared initial head; entries=n removal; refs= length-prefixed encoding and cross-actor unauthorised-ref outcome; deterministic genesis ledger root plus reachable-predecessor rejection; parent-role validation by object type. Then attack the unverified claims: that a profile commit's tree retains the ruleset under gc with the ledger as sole ref (measured only by the author); that parent-role validation by object type is cheaply computable; that rejecting a root with a ledger entry reachable anywhere in its parent graph is computable and bounded on a long ledger; that the genesis descriptor actually carries an initial head to anchor the base chain at the root, and what happens if it does not; that the length-prefixed refs encoding survives a delimiter-bearing ref name; and that the creator of a ref is determinable at all, since the unauthorised-ref remedy depends on it. Verify nothing downstream still depends on the removed entries field. Re-audit all spike cases for the cannot-fail class and for repaired-rule-with-surviving-old-sentence. Report APPROVED or CHANGES-REQUESTED against this exact head with verbatim full event ids.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}